{"task_id": "HumanEval/13", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n# Build & package metadata for the gcd_app project.\n[project]\nname = \"gcd-app\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A Python library, CLI, and HTTP API for computing GCD using multiple algorithms.\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }]\ndependencies = [\n    \"fastapi>=0.104.1\",\n    \"uvicorn[standard]>=0.24.0.post1\",\n    \"pydantic-settings>=2.1.0\",\n    \"typer>=0.9.0\", # For CLI, more robust than bare argparse for large CLI apps\n    \"loguru>=0.7.2\", # For logging as per design\n]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.10\"\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\n\n[project.scripts]\ngcd-cli = \"gcd_app.cli:main\"\n\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\npythonpath = [\"src\"]\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n```\n\n```\n# requirements.txt\n# Quick install list for production and development dependencies.\nfastapi>=0.104.1\nuvicorn[standard]>=0.24.0.post1\npydantic-settings>=2.1.0\ntyper>=0.9.0\nloguru>=0.7.2\n\n# Development dependencies\npytest>=7.4.3\nhttpx>=0.25.1 # For testing FastAPI app\n```\n\n```markdown\n# README.md\n# GCD Application\n\nThis project provides a Python library, a command-line interface (CLI), and an HTTP API for computing the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two integers using multiple algorithms.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Multiple Algorithms**: Supports Euclidean (default) and Binary (Stein's) algorithms.\n- **Pluggable**: Easily extend with new GCD algorithms.\n- **Caching**: Optional SQLite-based caching for performance.\n- **API Interfaces**:\n    - **Library API**: `GCDService` for programmatic access.\n    - **CLI**: `gcd-cli` command for terminal use.\n    - **HTTP API**: RESTful endpoints using FastAPI.\n- **Automated Tests**: Comprehensive test suite ensuring correctness.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\ngit clone <repository-url>\ncd gcd-app\npip install -r requirements.txt\n# Or using poetry\n# poetry install\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nCompute GCD:\n```bash\ngcd-cli compute 25 15\n# Output: GCD(25, 15) = 5 [algorithm=euclidean, duration=...ms]\n\ngcd-cli compute 100 75 --algorithm binary\n# Output: GCD(100, 75) = 25 [algorithm=binary, duration=...ms]\n\ngcd-cli compute 0 0\n# Output: GCD(0, 0) = 0 [algorithm=euclidean, duration=...ms]\n```\n\nTo enable caching for CLI:\n```bash\nGCD_CACHE_ENABLED=true gcd-cli compute 25 15\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nStart the API server (default port 8000):\n```bash\nuvicorn src.gcd_app.api:create_app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nOnce the server is running, you can interact with it:\n\n**POST /gcd**\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"http://localhost:8000/gcd\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"a\": 25, \"b\": 15, \"algorithm\": \"euclidean\"}'\n# Response: {\"a\":25,\"b\":15,\"gcd\":5,\"algorithm\":\"euclidean\",\"duration_ms\":0.123,\"cached\":false}\n```\n\n**GET /gcd/{a}/{b}**\n\n```bash\ncurl \"http://localhost:8000/gcd/100/75?algorithm=binary\"\n# Response: {\"a\":100,\"b\":75,\"gcd\":25,\"algorithm\":\"binary\",\"duration_ms\":0.045,\"cached\":false}\n```\n\nTo enable caching or configure API key:\n```bash\nGCD_CACHE_ENABLED=true GCD_API_KEY=\"secret-key\" uvicorn src.gcd_app.api:create_app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\nThen use `X-API-Key: secret-key` header for API requests.\n\n### Library Usage\n\n```python\nfrom gcd_app.config import AppConfig\nfrom gcd_app.algorithms import EuclideanGCD, BinaryGCD\nfrom gcd_app.repository import CacheRepository\nfrom gcd_app.services import GCDService\n\n# Configure the app\nconfig = AppConfig(\n    cache_enabled=True,\n    db_path=\"./data/my_cache.db\"\n)\n\n# Initialize algorithms\nalgorithms = {\n    EuclideanGCD.name: EuclideanGCD(),\n    BinaryGCD.name: BinaryGCD(),\n}\n\n# Initialize repository (optional)\nrepository = CacheRepository(config.db_path) if config.cache_enabled else None\n\n# Initialize the service\ngcd_service = GCDService(algorithms, repository, config)\n\n# Compute GCD\nresult = gcd_service.compute(a=36, b=48, algorithm=\"euclidean\")\nprint(f\"GCD({result.a}, {result.b}) = {result.gcd} (cached: {result.cached}, duration: {result.duration_ms:.2f}ms)\")\n\n# Compute with caching enabled (first time)\nresult1 = gcd_service.compute(a=50, b=75, use_cache=True)\nprint(f\"First compute: {result1.gcd}, cached: {result1.cached}\")\n\n# Compute again, should be cached\nresult2 = gcd_service.compute(a=50, b=75, use_cache=True)\nprint(f\"Second compute: {result2.gcd}, cached: {result2.cached}\")\n\nif repository:\n    repository.close()\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\nConfiguration can be set via environment variables:\n- `GCD_DB_PATH`: Path to the SQLite cache database (default: `./data/gcd_cache.db`)\n- `GCD_CACHE_ENABLED`: Set to `true` to enable caching (default: `false`)\n- `GCD_API_KEY`: Set an API key for HTTP API authentication (default: `None`)\n- `GCD_HOST`: Host for the HTTP API (default: `0.0.0.0`)\n- `GCD_PORT`: Port for the HTTP API (default: `8000`)\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\n```bash\npytest src/gcd_app/tests/\n```\n\n### CI/CD\n\nThe project uses GitHub Actions for continuous integration. See `.github/workflows/ci.yml` for details.\n```\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: CI/CD\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n      - develop\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n      - develop\n\njobs:\n  build-and-test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - name: Checkout code\n      uses: actions/checkout@v3\n\n    - name: Set up Python 3.10\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n      with:\n        python-version: '3.10'\n\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: |\n        python -m pip install --upgrade pip\n        pip install -r requirements.txt\n        pip install setuptools  # Ensure setuptools is available for package installation\n\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: |\n        pytest src/gcd_app/tests/\n\n    - name: Lint with flake8 (optional)\n      run: |\n        pip install flake8\n        flake8 src/\n```\n\n```sql\n-- docs/migration.sql\n-- SQL to create the gcd_cache table for SQLite.\nBEGIN;\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS gcd_cache (\n  a INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  b INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  algorithm TEXT NOT NULL,\n  result INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  computed_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY(a,b,algorithm)\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_gcd_cache_ab_alg ON gcd_cache(a,b,algorithm);\n\nCOMMIT;\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/__init__.py\n# Package metadata and initialization.\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/config.py\n# Central configuration dataclass for the application.\nfrom pydantic_settings import BaseSettings, SettingsConfigDict\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n# Define default paths and settings.\nDEFAULT_DB_PATH = Path(\"./data/gcd_cache.db\").resolve()\nDEFAULT_HOST = \"0.0.0.0\"\nDEFAULT_PORT = 8000\n\nclass AppConfig(BaseSettings):\n    \"\"\"\n    Application configuration loaded from environment variables or defaults.\n    Environment variables should be prefixed with GCD_ (e.g., GCD_DB_PATH).\n    \"\"\"\n    model_config = SettingsConfigDict(env_prefix='GCD_', env_file='.env', extra='ignore')\n\n    db_path: Path = DEFAULT_DB_PATH\n    cache_enabled: bool = False\n    api_key: Optional[str] = None\n    host: str = DEFAULT_HOST\n    port: int = DEFAULT_PORT\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_env(cls) -> \"AppConfig\":\n        \"\"\"Builds config from environment variables or defaults.\"\"\"\n        return cls()\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        \"\"\"Ensure parent directory for DB path exists.\"\"\"\n        if self.db_path:\n            self.db_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/exceptions.py\n# Custom exception types for domain-specific errors.\n\nclass InputValidationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input values.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass CacheError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for issues interacting with the cache repository.\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/models.py\n# Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) and type definitions.\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass GCDRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Represents an incoming GCD computation request.\"\"\"\n    a: int\n    b: int\n    algorithm: Optional[str] = None\n\nclass GCDResult(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Represents the result of a GCD computation.\"\"\"\n    a: int\n    b: int\n    gcd: int\n    algorithm: str\n    duration_ms: float\n    cached: bool\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/algorithms.py\n# GCD algorithm interface and concrete implementations.\nfrom typing import Protocol\n\n# Default algorithm name.\nDEFAULT_ALGORITHM = \"euclidean\"\n\nclass IGCDAlgorithm(Protocol):\n    \"\"\"Interface for GCD algorithms.\"\"\"\n    name: str\n\n    def compute(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the GCD of two integers.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\nclass EuclideanGCD:\n    \"\"\"Implements the Euclidean algorithm for GCD.\"\"\"\n    name = \"euclidean\"\n\n    def compute(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the GCD using the iterative Euclidean algorithm.\n        Handles zeros and negative numbers correctly, returning a non-negative result.\n        \"\"\"\n        a, b = abs(a), abs(b)\n        if a == 0 and b == 0:\n            return 0  # Business rule: gcd(0,0) = 0\n        while b:\n            a, b = b, a % b\n        return a\n\nclass BinaryGCD:\n    \"\"\"Implements Stein's (Binary) algorithm for GCD.\"\"\"\n    name = \"binary\"\n\n    def compute(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the GCD using Stein's Binary algorithm.\n        Handles zeros and negative numbers correctly, returning a non-negative result.\n        \"\"\"\n        a, b = abs(a), abs(b)\n        if a == 0:\n            return b\n        if b == 0:\n            return a\n        if a == 0 and b == 0:\n            return 0  # Business rule: gcd(0,0) = 0\n\n        shift = 0\n        while ((a | b) & 1) == 0: # While both are even\n            a >>= 1\n            b >>= 1\n            shift += 1\n\n        while (a & 1) == 0: # Make a odd\n            a >>= 1\n\n        while b != 0:\n            while (b & 1) == 0: # Make b odd\n                b >>= 1\n            if a > b:\n                a, b = b, a\n            b = (b - a) >> 1\n        return a << shift\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/repository.py\n# Cache repository adapter for SQLite.\nimport sqlite3\nimport datetime\nfrom typing import Optional, Tuple\nfrom loguru import logger\n\nfrom gcd_app.exceptions import CacheError\n\nclass CacheRepository:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages caching of GCD results in an SQLite database.\n    Ensures schema exists and normalizes (a,b) for consistent caching.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str):\n        self.db_path = db_path\n        self.conn: Optional[sqlite3.Connection] = None\n        self._connect()\n        self.ensure_schema()\n\n    def _connect(self):\n        \"\"\"Establishes a connection to the SQLite database.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            self.conn = sqlite3.connect(self.db_path, check_same_thread=False)\n            logger.info(f\"Connected to SQLite cache database: {self.db_path}\")\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to connect to SQLite database {self.db_path}: {e}\")\n            self.conn = None\n            raise CacheError(f\"DB connection failed: {e}\")\n\n    def ensure_schema(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Ensures the cache table schema exists in the database.\"\"\"\n        if not self.conn:\n            logger.warning(\"No database connection, cannot ensure schema.\")\n            return\n\n        try:\n            cursor = self.conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS gcd_cache (\n                    a INTEGER NOT NULL,\n                    b INTEGER NOT NULL,\n                    algorithm TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    result INTEGER NOT NULL,\n                    computed_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n                    PRIMARY KEY(a,b,algorithm)\n                );\n            \"\"\")\n            cursor.execute(\"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_gcd_cache_ab_alg ON gcd_cache(a,b,algorithm);\")\n            self.conn.commit()\n            logger.info(\"GCD cache schema ensured.\")\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to ensure schema for {self.db_path}: {e}\")\n            raise CacheError(f\"Schema creation failed: {e}\")\n\n    def _normalize_inputs(self, a: int, b: int) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Normalizes inputs (absolute values, min/max order) for consistent caching.\"\"\"\n        a, b = abs(a), abs(b)\n        return (min(a, b), max(a, b))\n\n    def get(self, a: int, b: int, algorithm: str) -> Optional[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieves a cached GCD result.\n        Returns the result if found, otherwise None.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not self.conn:\n            logger.warning(\"Cache repository not connected, cannot get data.\")\n            return None\n        \n        normalized_a, normalized_b = self._normalize_inputs(a, b)\n        try:\n            cursor = self.conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\n                \"SELECT result FROM gcd_cache WHERE a = ? AND b = ? AND algorithm = ?\",\n                (normalized_a, normalized_b, algorithm.lower())\n            )\n            row = cursor.fetchone()\n            if row:\n                logger.debug(f\"Cache hit for ({a}, {b}, {algorithm})\")\n                return row[0]\n            logger.debug(f\"Cache miss for ({a}, {b}, {algorithm})\")\n            return None\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Error reading from cache for ({a}, {b}, {algorithm}): {e}\")\n            raise CacheError(f\"Error retrieving from cache: {e}\") from e\n\n    def set(self, a: int, b: int, algorithm: str, result: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Stores a computed GCD result in the cache.\n        Overwrites existing entries for the same (a,b,algorithm).\n        \"\"\"\n        if not self.conn:\n            logger.warning(\"Cache repository not connected, cannot set data.\")\n            return\n\n        normalized_a, normalized_b = self._normalize_inputs(a, b)\n        try:\n            cursor = self.conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\n                \"\"\"\n                INSERT OR REPLACE INTO gcd_cache (a, b, algorithm, result, computed_at)\n                VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\n                \"\"\",\n                (normalized_a, normalized_b, algorithm.lower(), result, datetime.datetime.now())\n            )\n            self.conn.commit()\n            logger.debug(f\"Cache set for ({a}, {b}, {algorithm}) = {result}\")\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Error writing to cache for ({a}, {b}, {algorithm}) = {result}: {e}\")\n            raise CacheError(f\"Error setting cache: {e}\") from e\n\n    def close(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Closes the database connection.\"\"\"\n        if self.conn:\n            self.conn.close()\n            self.conn = None\n            logger.info(\"SQLite cache connection closed.\")\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/services.py\n# Business orchestration of GCD computation, including validation, caching, and algorithm selection.\nfrom time import perf_counter\nfrom typing import Dict, Optional, Any\nfrom loguru import logger\n\nfrom gcd_app.models import GCDResult\nfrom gcd_app.algorithms import IGCDAlgorithm, DEFAULT_ALGORITHM\nfrom gcd_app.repository import CacheRepository\nfrom gcd_app.config import AppConfig\nfrom gcd_app.utils import validate_int, timer\nfrom gcd_app.exceptions import InputValidationError, CacheError\n\nclass GCDService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Orchestrates GCD computations, handling input validation,\n    algorithm selection, optional caching, and result assembly.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self,\n                 algorithms: Dict[str, IGCDAlgorithm],\n                 repository: Optional[CacheRepository],\n                 config: AppConfig):\n        self.algorithms = algorithms\n        self.repo = repository\n        self.config = config\n        logger.info(f\"GCDService initialized with algorithms: {list(algorithms.keys())}\")\n        if self.config.cache_enabled and self.repo:\n            logger.info(f\"Caching enabled. DB path: {self.repo.db_path}\")\n        else:\n            logger.info(\"Caching disabled or repository not provided.\")\n\n    def compute(self,\n                a: Any,\n                b: Any,\n                algorithm: Optional[str] = None,\n                use_cache: Optional[bool] = None) -> GCDResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the GCD of two integers using a specified algorithm and optional caching.\n        Raises InputValidationError for invalid inputs.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            # 1. Validate inputs\n            int_a = validate_int(a)\n            int_b = validate_int(b)\n        except InputValidationError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Invalid input received: {e}\")\n            raise\n\n        # 2. Resolve algorithm\n        alg_key = (algorithm or DEFAULT_ALGORITHM).lower()\n        if alg_key not in self.algorithms:\n            raise InputValidationError(f\"Algorithm '{alg_key}' not supported. Available: {list(self.algorithms.keys())}\")\n        algo = self.algorithms[alg_key]\n\n        actual_use_cache = use_cache if use_cache is not None else self.config.cache_enabled\n        cached_result: Optional[int] = None\n        \n        # 3. If caching is enabled and repository is available, consult cache\n        if actual_use_cache and self.repo:\n            try:\n                cached_result = self.repo.get(int_a, int_b, alg_key)\n                if cached_result is not None:\n                    logger.info(f\"Cache hit for GCD({int_a}, {int_b}) with {alg_key}. Result: {cached_result}\")\n                    return GCDResult(a=int_a, b=int_b, gcd=cached_result, algorithm=alg_key, duration_ms=0.0, cached=True)\n            except CacheError as e:\n                logger.warning(f\"Cache lookup failed, proceeding with computation: {e}\")\n\n        # 4. Compute GCD if not cached\n        logger.info(f\"Computing GCD({int_a}, {int_b}) using {alg_key} algorithm.\")\n        start_time = perf_counter()\n        result = algo.compute(int_a, int_b)\n        duration_ms = (perf_counter() - start_time) * 1000.0\n        logger.info(f\"GCD({int_a}, {int_b}) computed as {result} in {duration_ms:.2f}ms using {alg_key}.\")\n\n        # 5. Save result to cache if enabled and repository is available\n        if actual_use_cache and self.repo:\n            try:\n                self.repo.set(int_a, int_b, alg_key, result)\n                logger.debug(f\"Result for GCD({int_a}, {int_b}) with {alg_key} cached successfully.\")\n            except CacheError as e:\n                logger.warning(f\"Failed to save result to cache: {e}\")\n        \n        # 6. Return DTO\n        return GCDResult(a=int_a, b=int_b, gcd=result, algorithm=alg_key, duration_ms=duration_ms, cached=False)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/controllers.py\n# Adapters between the GCDService and presentation layers (HTTP API, CLI).\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\nimport sys\nfrom loguru import logger\nimport typer\n\nfrom gcd_app.services import GCDService\nfrom gcd_app.models import GCDRequest, GCDResult\nfrom gcd_app.exceptions import InputValidationError\nfrom gcd_app.utils import format_result_for_cli\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Adapts HTTP requests to the GCDService and formats responses for the API.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: GCDService):\n        self.service = service\n\n    def compute_handler(self, request: GCDRequest) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Handles an API request to compute GCD.\n        Calls the GCDService and returns a dictionary suitable for JSON response.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            result = self.service.compute(request.a, request.b, request.algorithm)\n            return result.model_dump()\n        except InputValidationError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"API input validation error: {e}\")\n            raise # Re-raise for FastAPI exception handling\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Unexpected API error during GCD computation: {e}\")\n            raise # Re-raise for FastAPI exception handling\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Adapts command-line arguments to the GCDService and formats output for the console.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: GCDService):\n        self.service = service\n\n    def run(self, a: int, b: int, algorithm: str, no_cache: bool) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Executes the GCD computation based on CLI arguments and prints the result.\n        Returns an exit code.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            # Note: `no_cache` from CLI means `use_cache=False`.\n            # If `no_cache` is true, then `use_cache` should be explicitly false.\n            # Otherwise, it defers to the service's default/config.\n            use_cache = not no_cache if no_cache is not None else None\n            \n            result = self.service.compute(a, b, algorithm, use_cache=use_cache)\n            print(format_result_for_cli(result))\n            return 0  # Success exit code\n        except InputValidationError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"CLI input validation error: {e}\")\n            typer.echo(f\"Error: {e}\", err=True)\n            return 1  # Non-zero exit code for invalid arguments\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Unexpected CLI error during GCD computation: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            typer.echo(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", err=True)\n            return 1  # Non-zero exit code for runtime error\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/api.py\n# FastAPI application factory and route bindings.\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Depends, status\nfrom fastapi.security import APIKeyHeader\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any\nfrom loguru import logger\n\nfrom gcd_app.config import AppConfig\nfrom gcd_app.services import GCDService\nfrom gcd_app.controllers import APIController\nfrom gcd_app.algorithms import EuclideanGCD, BinaryGCD, DEFAULT_ALGORITHM\nfrom gcd_app.repository import CacheRepository\nfrom gcd_app.models import GCDRequest\nfrom gcd_app.exceptions import InputValidationError, CacheError\n\napi_key_header = APIKeyHeader(name=\"X-API-Key\", auto_error=False)\n\nasync def verify_api_key(api_key: str = Depends(api_key_header), config: AppConfig = Depends(lambda: create_app().extra[\"config\"])):\n    \"\"\"Dependency to verify API key if configured.\"\"\"\n    if config.api_key:\n        if not api_key or api_key != config.api_key:\n            logger.warning(\"Unauthorized access attempt: Invalid or missing API Key.\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED, detail=\"Invalid or missing API Key\")\n    return api_key\n\ndef create_app(config: Optional[AppConfig] = None) -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates and configures the FastAPI application instance.\n    Initializes services and binds API routes.\n    \"\"\"\n    config = config or AppConfig.from_env()\n    app = FastAPI(\n        title=\"GCD App\",\n        description=\"A service to compute Greatest Common Divisor using various algorithms.\",\n        version=\"0.1.0\"\n    )\n\n    # Initialize domain and infrastructure components\n    algorithms = {\n        EuclideanGCD.name: EuclideanGCD(),\n        BinaryGCD.name: BinaryGCD(),\n    }\n    \n    repository = None\n    if config.cache_enabled:\n        try:\n            repository = CacheRepository(str(config.db_path))\n        except CacheError:\n            logger.critical(\"Failed to initialize CacheRepository. Caching will be disabled.\")\n            config.cache_enabled = False # Explicitly disable if repo failed\n    \n    gcd_service = GCDService(algorithms, repository, config)\n    api_controller = APIController(gcd_service)\n\n    # Store components in app.extra for dependency injection or access if needed\n    app.extra[\"config\"] = config\n    app.extra[\"gcd_service\"] = gcd_service\n    app.extra[\"api_controller\"] = api_controller\n    app.extra[\"repository\"] = repository # Keep reference for graceful shutdown\n\n    # Define API routes\n    @app.post(\"/gcd\", response_model=Dict[str, Any], status_code=status.HTTP_200_OK, dependencies=[Depends(verify_api_key)])\n    async def post_compute_gcd(request: GCDRequest) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes GCD via POST request with JSON payload.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            return api_controller.compute_handler(request)\n        except InputValidationError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=str(e))\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"Internal server error during POST /gcd\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"Internal Server Error\")\n\n    @app.get(\"/gcd/{a}/{b}\", response_model=Dict[str, Any], status_code=status.HTTP_200_OK, dependencies=[Depends(verify_api_key)])\n    async def get_compute_gcd(a: int, b: int, algorithm: Optional[str] = None) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes GCD via GET request with path parameters.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            request = GCDRequest(a=a, b=b, algorithm=algorithm)\n            return api_controller.compute_handler(request)\n        except InputValidationError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=str(e))\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"Internal server error during GET /gcd/{a}/{b}\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"Internal Server Error\")\n\n    @app.on_event(\"shutdown\")\n    async def shutdown_event():\n        \"\"\"Handle application shutdown, close repository connection.\"\"\"\n        repo = app.extra.get(\"repository\")\n        if repo:\n            repo.close()\n            logger.info(\"Application shutdown: CacheRepository connection closed.\")\n\n    return app\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/cli.py\n# Console entrypoint for the gcd-cli command.\nfrom typing import Optional, Sequence\nimport typer\nfrom loguru import logger\n\nfrom gcd_app.config import AppConfig\nfrom gcd_app.algorithms import EuclideanGCD, BinaryGCD, DEFAULT_ALGORITHM\nfrom gcd_app.repository import CacheRepository\nfrom gcd_app.services import GCDService\nfrom gcd_app.controllers import CLIController\nfrom gcd_app.exceptions import CacheError\n\n# Initialize Typer app\napp = typer.Typer(help=\"GCD CLI application for computing Greatest Common Divisor.\")\n\n@app.command()\ndef compute(\n    a: int = typer.Argument(..., help=\"First integer.\"),\n    b: int = typer.Argument(..., help=\"Second integer.\"),\n    algorithm: Optional[str] = typer.Option(DEFAULT_ALGORITHM, \"--algorithm\", \"-a\", help=\"Algorithm to use (euclidean, binary).\"),\n    no_cache: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--no-cache\", \"-nc\", help=\"Do not use cache for this computation.\"),\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the Greatest Common Divisor of two integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    config = AppConfig.from_env()\n    \n    algorithms = {\n        EuclideanGCD.name: EuclideanGCD(),\n        BinaryGCD.name: BinaryGCD(),\n    }\n    \n    repository = None\n    if config.cache_enabled and not no_cache: # Only try to init repo if caching is generally enabled and not explicitly disabled for this call\n        try:\n            repository = CacheRepository(str(config.db_path))\n        except CacheError:\n            logger.critical(\"Failed to initialize CacheRepository. Caching will be disabled for this run.\")\n            # config.cache_enabled = False # No need to modify config as `use_cache` param will handle it.\n            repository = None\n    \n    gcd_service = GCDService(algorithms, repository, config)\n    cli_controller = CLIController(gcd_service)\n    \n    exit_code = cli_controller.run(a, b, algorithm, no_cache)\n    \n    if repository:\n        repository.close()\n    \n    typer.Exit(code=exit_code)\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[Sequence[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point for the CLI application.\n    \"\"\"\n    logger.remove() # Remove default logger\n    logger.add(sys.stderr, level=\"INFO\") # Add a stderr logger for CLI output\n\n    # Typer handles argv parsing, so we just call the app directly.\n    # It will manage the exit codes through typer.Exit\n    app()\n    return 0 # Should not be reached, typer.Exit handles termination\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/utils.py\n# Utility functions for common tasks like input validation, timing, and formatting.\nimport time\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom loguru import logger\n\nfrom gcd_app.exceptions import InputValidationError\nfrom gcd_app.models import GCDResult\n\ndef validate_int(value: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if a value can be converted to an integer.\n    Raises InputValidationError if not a valid integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        if isinstance(value, bool): # Disallow boolean as int to avoid surprises\n            raise TypeError(\"Boolean value is not a valid integer.\")\n        return int(value)\n    except (ValueError, TypeError) as e:\n        raise InputValidationError(f\"Invalid input: '{value}' cannot be converted to an integer. Details: {e}\")\n\n@contextmanager\ndef timer() -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    A context manager to measure the execution time of a block of code in milliseconds.\n    Yields the duration in milliseconds.\n    \"\"\"\n    start_time = time.perf_counter()\n    try:\n        yield\n    finally:\n        end_time = time.perf_counter()\n        duration_ms = (end_time - start_time) * 1000.0\n        # This context manager just yields; the consumer can log the result.\n        # logger.debug(f\"Operation took {duration_ms:.2f} ms\") # Example usage in service\n        return duration_ms # Not directly returned by context manager, but can be captured\n\ndef format_result_for_cli(result: GCDResult) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Formats a GCDResult object into a human-readable string for CLI output.\n    \"\"\"\n    cache_status = \"cached\" if result.cached else \"computed\"\n    return (f\"GCD({result.a}, {result.b}) = {result.gcd} \"\n            f\"[algorithm={result.algorithm}, duration={result.duration_ms:.2f}ms, status={cache_status}]\")\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_app/tests/__init__.py\n# Marker for the tests package.\n```"}
