{"task_id": "HumanEval/14", "solution": "```python\n# LICENSE\n#\n# MIT License\n#\n# Copyright (c) 2024 Your Name or Company\n#\n# Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n# of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n# in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n# to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n# copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n# furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n#\n# The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n# copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n#\n# THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n# IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n# FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n# AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n# LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n# OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n# SOFTWARE.\n```\n```markdown\n# stringutils\n\nA Python utility for generating all prefixes of a given string, from shortest to longest.\nIt provides a library function, a command-line interface (CLI), and an optional HTTP API.\n\n## Features\n\n- **`all_prefixes(string)` function**: Directly callable for core logic.\n- **`PrefixService`**: Handles validation, caching, and generation logic.\n- **CLI Tool (`prefixgen`)**: Generate prefixes from the command line, with options to save output.\n- **HTTP API (`/prefixes`)**: Optional Flask-based endpoint for service consumption.\n- **Pluggable Repositories**: Supports in-memory LRU cache and file-backed JSON persistence.\n- **Configurable**: Max input length, cache size, and persistence file are configurable.\n\n## Installation\n\nThis project uses Poetry for dependency management and packaging.\n\n1. **Clone the repository:**\n   ```bash\n   git clone https://github.com/your-org/stringutils.git\n   cd stringutils\n   ```\n\n2. **Install with Poetry:**\n   If you don't have Poetry, install it first: `pip install poetry`.\n   Then, install project dependencies:\n   ```bash\n   poetry install\n   ```\n\n   To include the optional HTTP API dependencies (Flask):\n   ```bash\n   poetry install --with http\n   ```\n\n## Usage\n\n### 1. Library Function\n\nYou can directly use the core `all_prefixes` function:\n\n```python\nfrom stringutils import all_prefixes\n\nprefixes = all_prefixes(\"hello\")\nprint(prefixes)  # Output: ['h', 'he', 'hel', 'hell', 'hello']\n```\n\nFor more advanced usage with validation, caching, and dependency injection:\n\n```python\nfrom stringutils.config import get_config\nfrom stringutils.core import PrefixGenerator\nfrom stringutils.repositories import InMemoryCacheRepository\nfrom stringutils.services import PrefixService\nfrom stringutils.validators import StringValidator\n\nconfig = get_config()\ngenerator = PrefixGenerator()\nvalidator = StringValidator()\nrepository = InMemoryCacheRepository(max_size=config[\"DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE\"])\nservice = PrefixService(generator, repository, validator, config)\n\nresult = service.generate(\"world\")\nprint(result.prefixes)\nprint(f\"Source: {result.source}, Generated At: {result.generated_at}\")\n```\n\n### 2. Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nThe CLI tool `prefixgen` is installed as part of the package.\n\n```bash\n# Generate prefixes for a string\nprefixgen --string \"example\"\n# Output: [\"e\", \"ex\", \"exa\", \"exam\", \"examp\", \"example\"]\n\n# Generate prefixes and save to a file\nprefixgen -s \"longstring\" -o output.json\n\n# Bypass cache (e.g., to force regeneration or debug)\nprefixgen -s \"another\" --no-cache\n\n# For help\nprefixgen --help\n```\n\n### 3. HTTP API (Optional)\n\nIf you installed with `--with http`, you can run the HTTP server.\n\n```bash\n# Run the server (ensure you are in the project root)\n./scripts/run_local_server.sh\n```\n\nThen access the API:\n\n```bash\n# Example using curl\ncurl \"http://127.0.0.1:5000/prefixes?string=api\"\n# Expected JSON output:\n# {\n#   \"meta\": {\n#     \"generated_at\": \"...\",\n#     \"input_length\": 3,\n#     \"source\": \"generated\"\n#   },\n#   \"prefixes\": [\"a\", \"ap\", \"api\"]\n# }\n\n# With no_cache option\ncurl \"http://127.0.0.1:5000/prefixes?string=api&no_cache=true\"\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\nConfiguration values can be overridden via environment variables:\n\n- `STRINGUTILS_MAX_INPUT_LENGTH`: Maximum allowed length for input strings (default: 100000).\n- `STRINGUTILS_DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE`: Max items in in-memory cache (default: 1024).\n- `STRINGUTILS_DEFAULT_PERSIST_FILE`: Path for `FileCacheRepository` (default: `prefix_cache.json`).\n\nExample:\n```bash\nexport STRINGUTILS_MAX_INPUT_LENGTH=5000\nprefixgen -s \"test\"\n```\n\n## Development\n\nRun tests:\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\n\nLinting:\n```bash\npoetry run flake8 src\n```\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"stringutils\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A Python utility for generating string prefixes with CLI and optional HTTP API.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nlicense = \"MIT\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \"^3.9\"\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.2.0\"\nflake8 = \"^7.0.0\"\nrequests = \"^2.31.0\" # For integration tests\n\n[tool.poetry.group.http]\noptional = true\ndependencies = { flask = \"^3.0.3\" }\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nprefixgen = \"stringutils.__main__:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nstringutils - A utility for generating string prefixes.\n\nThis package provides a core function `all_prefixes` and a robust\nservice layer with caching, validation, CLI, and HTTP API capabilities.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .core import all_prefixes, PrefixGenerator\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, RepositoryError\nfrom .models import PrefixResult\nfrom .services import PrefixService\nfrom .validators import StringValidator\nfrom .repositories import IRepository, InMemoryCacheRepository, FileCacheRepository\nfrom .config import get_config\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"all_prefixes\",\n    \"PrefixGenerator\",\n    \"PrefixResult\",\n    \"PrefixService\",\n    \"StringValidator\",\n    \"IRepository\",\n    \"InMemoryCacheRepository\",\n    \"FileCacheRepository\",\n    \"InvalidInputError\",\n    \"RepositoryError\",\n    \"get_config\",\n]\n\ntry:\n    from .controllers import HTTPController\n    __all__.append(\"HTTPController\")\nexcept ImportError:\n    # Flask is an optional dependency, so HTTPController might not be available\n    pass\n\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/config.py\nimport os\n\n# Default configuration values\nMAX_INPUT_LENGTH: int = 100000\nDEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE: int = 1024\nDEFAULT_PERSIST_FILE: str = \"prefix_cache.json\"\n\ndef get_config() -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Reads configuration from environment variables, with defaults.\"\"\"\n    config = {\n        \"MAX_INPUT_LENGTH\": int(os.getenv(\"STRINGUTILS_MAX_INPUT_LENGTH\", MAX_INPUT_LENGTH)),\n        \"DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE\": int(os.getenv(\"STRINGUTILS_DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE\", DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE)),\n        \"DEFAULT_PERSIST_FILE\": os.getenv(\"STRINGUTILS_DEFAULT_PERSIST_FILE\", DEFAULT_PERSIST_FILE),\n    }\n    return config\n\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/exceptions.py\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\nclass RepositoryError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for repository-related failures.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/models.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\n\n@dataclass\nclass PrefixResult:\n    \"\"\"Data transfer object for prefix generation results.\"\"\"\n    prefixes: List[str]\n    source: str  # e.g., 'cache' or 'generated'\n    generated_at: str  # ISO8601 timestamp string\n    input_length: int\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Converts the PrefixResult instance to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"prefixes\": self.prefixes,\n            \"source\": self.source,\n            \"generated_at\": self.generated_at,\n            \"input_length\": self.input_length,\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, d: Dict[str, Any]) -> \"PrefixResult\":\n        \"\"\"Creates a PrefixResult instance from a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return cls(\n            prefixes=d[\"prefixes\"],\n            source=d[\"source\"],\n            generated_at=d[\"generated_at\"],\n            input_length=d[\"input_length\"],\n        )\n\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/validators.py\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass StringValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates input strings based on type and length constraints.\"\"\"\n    def validate(self, string: str, max_length: int = None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Raises InvalidInputError if the string is not valid.\n        Checks if input is a string and its length is within limits.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(string, str):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n        if max_length is not None and len(string) > max_length:\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"String length exceeds maximum limit of {max_length} characters.\")\n\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/core.py\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef all_prefixes(string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list of all prefixes of the input string, from shortest to longest.\n    Assumes valid string input as per caller's validation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not string:\n        return []\n    return [string[:i] for i in range(1, len(string) + 1)]\n\nclass PrefixGenerator:\n    \"\"\"\n    A class-based wrapper for the all_prefixes function.\n    Provides a standardized interface for dependency injection.\n    \"\"\"\n    def generate(self, string: str) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Generates all prefixes for the given string using the core algorithm.\n        \"\"\"\n        return all_prefixes(string)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/repositories.py\nimport json\nimport os\nimport fcntl\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any, Protocol\n\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE, DEFAULT_PERSIST_FILE\nfrom .exceptions import RepositoryError\n\nclass IRepository(Protocol):\n    \"\"\"\n    Interface for data repositories, defining methods for caching/persistence.\n    \"\"\"\n    def get(self, key: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a value by its key.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    def set(self, key: str, value: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores a value associated with a key.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    def delete(self, key: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Deletes a value by its key.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\nclass InMemoryCacheRepository:\n    \"\"\"\n    An in-memory LRU cache implementation of IRepository.\n    It evicts the least recently used items when its size limit is reached.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, max_size: int = DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE):\n        if max_size <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Max size must be positive.\")\n        self._max_size = max_size\n        self._cache: OrderedDict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves an item from the cache and updates its recency.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            value = self._cache.pop(key)  # Remove and re-insert to mark as recently used\n            self._cache[key] = value\n            return value\n        except KeyError:\n            return None\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Error getting from in-memory cache: {e}\") from e\n\n    def set(self, key: str, value: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores an item in the cache, evicting LRU if size limit exceeded.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            if key in self._cache:\n                self._cache.pop(key)  # Remove old entry\n            self._cache[key] = value  # Add new entry (most recent)\n\n            while len(self._cache) > self._max_size:\n                self._cache.popitem(last=False)  # Remove least recently used\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Error setting in in-memory cache: {e}\") from e\n\n    def delete(self, key: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Deletes an item from the cache.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            if key in self._cache:\n                del self._cache[key]\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Error deleting from in-memory cache: {e}\") from e\n\nclass FileCacheRepository:\n    \"\"\"\n    A file-backed JSON cache implementation of IRepository.\n    Suitable for small caches; loads the entire file into memory for operations.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, file_path: str = DEFAULT_PERSIST_FILE):\n        self._file_path = file_path\n        self._cache: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n        self._load_data()\n\n    def _load_data(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Loads data from the JSON file into memory.\"\"\"\n        if not os.path.exists(self._file_path):\n            self._cache = {}\n            return\n\n        try:\n            with open(self._file_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                # Use fcntl for advisory file locking on Unix-like systems\n                try:\n                    fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_SH)\n                except AttributeError:\n                    # fcntl not available on Windows\n                    pass\n                self._cache = json.load(f)\n        except (IOError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Error loading cache from {self._file_path}: {e}\") from e\n        finally:\n            try:\n                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n            except (AttributeError, ValueError):\n                pass # Already unlocked or not available\n\n    def _save_data(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Saves data from memory to the JSON file atomically.\"\"\"\n        temp_file_path = f\"{self._file_path}.tmp\"\n        try:\n            with open(temp_file_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                try:\n                    fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX) # Exclusive lock\n                except AttributeError:\n                    pass\n                json.dump(self._cache, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n        except IOError as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Error writing to temporary cache file {temp_file_path}: {e}\") from e\n        finally:\n            try:\n                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n            except (AttributeError, ValueError):\n                pass\n\n        try:\n            os.replace(temp_file_path, self._file_path) # Atomic replace\n        except OSError as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Error replacing cache file {self._file_path}: {e}\") from e\n\n    def get(self, key: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves an item from the file-backed cache.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            return self._cache.get(key)\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Error getting from file cache: {e}\") from e\n\n    def set(self, key: str, value: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores an item in the file-backed cache and persists it.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            self._cache[key] = value\n            self._save_data()\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Error setting in file cache: {e}\") from e\n\n    def delete(self, key: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Deletes an item from the file-backed cache and persists the change.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            if key in self._cache:\n                del self._cache[key]\n                self._save_data()\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Error deleting from file cache: {e}\") from e\n\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/services.py\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport hashlib\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\nfrom .core import PrefixGenerator\nfrom .exceptions import RepositoryError, InvalidInputError\nfrom .models import PrefixResult\nfrom .repositories import IRepository\nfrom .validators import StringValidator\n\nclass PrefixService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Orchestrates validation, cache lookup, prefix generation, and result persistence.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self,\n                 generator: PrefixGenerator,\n                 repository: IRepository,\n                 validator: StringValidator,\n                 config: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.generator = generator\n        self.repository = repository\n        self.validator = validator\n        self.config = config\n\n    def generate(self, string: str, no_cache: bool = False) -> PrefixResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates the input string, attempts to retrieve prefixes from cache,\n        generates them if not found, and stores the result.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.validator.validate(string, max_length=self.config.get(\"MAX_INPUT_LENGTH\"))\n\n        key = self._make_cache_key(string)\n        \n        if not no_cache:\n            try:\n                cached_payload = self.repository.get(key)\n                if cached_payload:\n                    return PrefixResult.from_dict(cached_payload)\n            except RepositoryError as e:\n                # Log the error but proceed with generation if cache lookup fails\n                print(f\"Warning: Cache lookup failed for key '{key}': {e}\") # Or use a proper logger\n\n        try:\n            prefixes = self.generator.generate(string)\n            result = PrefixResult(\n                prefixes=prefixes,\n                source=\"generated\",\n                generated_at=datetime.utcnow().isoformat(timespec='seconds') + \"Z\",\n                input_length=len(string)\n            )\n            \n            # Store in cache even if no_cache was true for lookup, unless explicitly prevented by repo design.\n            # Here, we store it if it was a miss. If no_cache means *never* cache, add a flag.\n            # Current interpretation: no_cache is only for *retrieval* bypass.\n            try:\n                self.repository.set(key, result.to_dict())\n            except RepositoryError as e:\n                print(f\"Warning: Cache storage failed for key '{key}': {e}\") # Or use a proper logger\n            \n            return result\n        except InvalidInputError: # Should not happen if validator is correctly used upstream\n            raise\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to generate prefixes for string '{string}': {e}\") from e\n\n    def _make_cache_key(self, string: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Creates a deterministic cache key for the input string.\n        Uses SHA256 hash of the string to handle long inputs efficiently.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Ensure the string is encoded consistently for hashing\n        string_bytes = string.encode('utf-8')\n        hash_digest = hashlib.sha256(string_bytes).hexdigest()\n        return f\"prefix:{len(string)}:{hash_digest}\"\n\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/utils.py\nimport json\nfrom .models import PrefixResult\n\ndef json_serialize_prefix_result(result: PrefixResult) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Serializes a PrefixResult object into a compact JSON string.\n    \"\"\"\n    return json.dumps(result.to_dict(), ensure_ascii=False)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/controllers.py\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport json\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .services import PrefixService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, RepositoryError\nfrom .utils import json_serialize_prefix_result\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles command-line interface interactions for the prefix generator.\n    Parses arguments, calls the PrefixService, and prints/saves results.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: PrefixService):\n        self.service = service\n\n    def run_cli(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Executes the CLI logic, parsing arguments and invoking the service.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for errors).\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Generate all prefixes of a given string.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"-s\", \"--string\", type=str, required=True,\n            help=\"The input string to generate prefixes for.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"-o\", \"--out\", type=str,\n            help=\"Optional file path to save the JSON output.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--no-cache\", action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Bypass the cache and force regeneration.\"\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        try:\n            result = self.service.generate(args.string, no_cache=args.no_cache)\n            output_json = json_serialize_prefix_result(result)\n\n            if args.out:\n                with open(args.out, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                    f.write(output_json)\n                print(f\"Prefixes saved to {args.out}\")\n            else:\n                # Pretty print for stdout\n                parsed_output = json.loads(output_json)\n                print(json.dumps(parsed_output, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Invalid input exit code\n        except RepositoryError as e:\n            print(f\"Repository Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # General error exit code\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\ntry:\n    from flask import Flask, request, jsonify, Response\n    FLASK_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    FLASK_AVAILABLE = False\n    Flask = None # type: ignore\n    request = None # type: ignore\n    jsonify = None # type: ignore\n    Response = None # type: ignore\n\n\nclass HTTPController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides an optional Flask application with an HTTP endpoint\n    to generate string prefixes.\n    \"\"\"\n    def create_app(self, service: PrefixService) -> Flask:\n        \"\"\"\n        Creates and configures a Flask application with the /prefixes endpoint.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not FLASK_AVAILABLE:\n            raise ImportError(\"Flask is not installed. Install with `poetry install --with http`\")\n\n        app = Flask(__name__)\n\n        @app.route(\"/prefixes\", methods=[\"GET\"])\n        def prefixes() -> Response:\n            s: Optional[str] = request.args.get(\"string\")\n            no_cache_param: Optional[str] = request.args.get(\"no_cache\")\n            no_cache: bool = no_cache_param is not None and no_cache_param.lower() == 'true'\n\n            if s is None:\n                return jsonify({\"error\": \"Missing 'string' query parameter.\"}), 400\n\n            try:\n                result = service.generate(s, no_cache=no_cache)\n                # The design doc requests format {prefixes: [...], meta: {...}}\n                return jsonify({\n                    \"prefixes\": result.prefixes,\n                    \"meta\": {\n                        \"source\": result.source,\n                        \"generated_at\": result.generated_at,\n                        \"input_length\": result.input_length\n                    }\n                }), 200\n            except InvalidInputError as e:\n                return jsonify({\"error\": f\"Invalid input: {e.message}\"}), 400\n            except RepositoryError as e:\n                # Log repository error for internal debugging\n                app.logger.error(f\"Repository error: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n                return jsonify({\"error\": \"Internal server error due to data storage/retrieval issue.\"}), 500\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Log other unexpected errors\n                app.logger.error(f\"Unexpected error: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n                return jsonify({\"error\": \"An unexpected internal server error occurred.\"}), 500\n        \n        return app\n\n```\n```python\n# src/stringutils/__main__.py\nimport sys\n\nfrom .config import get_config\nfrom .core import PrefixGenerator\nfrom .controllers import CLIController\nfrom .repositories import InMemoryCacheRepository, FileCacheRepository\nfrom .services import PrefixService\nfrom .validators import StringValidator\n\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point for the CLI application.\n    Initializes dependencies and runs the CLI controller.\n    \"\"\"\n    config = get_config()\n\n    # Core components\n    generator = PrefixGenerator()\n    validator = StringValidator()\n\n    # Choose repository based on configuration or environment (e.g., CLI option could be added)\n    # For simplicity, default to InMemoryCacheRepository, but FileCacheRepository is available.\n    # To use FileCacheRepository:\n    # repository = FileCacheRepository(file_path=config[\"DEFAULT_PERSIST_FILE\"])\n    repository = InMemoryCacheRepository(max_size=config[\"DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE\"])\n\n    # Service layer\n    service = PrefixService(\n        generator=generator,\n        repository=repository,\n        validator=validator,\n        config=config\n    )\n\n    # Presentation layer\n    cli_controller = CLIController(service=service)\n\n    # Run the CLI application\n    sys.exit(cli_controller.run_cli(sys.argv[1:]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# scripts/run_local_server.sh\n#\n# Helper script to run the optional HTTP server locally.\n#\n# Usage:\n#   ./scripts/run_local_server.sh\n#\n# Ensure you have Flask installed:\n#   poetry install --with http\n#\n\n# Activate poetry environment if not already active\nif [ -z \"$VIRTUAL_ENV\" ]; then\n    echo \"Activating Poetry environment...\"\n    # Assuming poetry is in PATH and project root is current directory\n    source $(poetry env info --path)/bin/activate\nfi\n\n# Set FLASK_APP to the module containing the create_app function\nexport FLASK_APP=\"stringutils.controllers\"\n\n# Optional: Set a specific repository for the HTTP service\n# By default, it will use InMemoryCacheRepository defined in main.py if run\n# via flask run --app stringutils --debug\n# For a more specific setup like the CLI, we might need a custom run function\n# For this design, create_app expects a service, so we'll run it this way:\n# We need to explicitly call create_app and run it.\n# A simpler way with FLASK_APP and CLI entry would be:\n# flask run\n\n# For now, let's just instruct how to run with the default setup\necho \"Starting Flask development server...\"\necho \"Access at http://127.0.0.1:5000/prefixes?string=test\"\necho \"To use FileCacheRepository, modify src/stringutils/__main__.py or create a custom server script.\"\necho \"\"\necho \"Running `flask --app stringutils.controllers:create_app run` directly is not ideal as it doesn't inject service.\"\necho \"Instead, we can create a simple `app.py` or `wsgi.py` that configures and runs the app:\"\necho \"---\"\necho \"# app.py\"\necho \"from stringutils.config import get_config\"\necho \"from stringutils.core import PrefixGenerator\"\necho \"from stringutils.repositories import InMemoryCacheRepository\"\necho \"from stringutils.services import PrefixService\"\necho \"from stringutils.validators import StringValidator\"\necho \"from stringutils.controllers import HTTPController\"\necho \"\"\necho \"config = get_config()\"\necho \"generator = PrefixGenerator()\"\necho \"validator = StringValidator()\"\necho \"repository = InMemoryCacheRepository(max_size=config[\\\"DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE\\\"])\"\necho \"service = PrefixService(generator, repository, validator, config)\"\necho \"app = HTTPController().create_app(service)\"\necho \"\"\necho \"if __name__ == '__main__':\"\necho \"    app.run(debug=True)\"\necho \"---\"\necho \"\"\necho \"Then you can run: `python app.py`\"\necho \"For now, we'll demonstrate by running a simple flask app which assumes default service setup internally:\"\necho \"This requires `create_app` to be configurable or context-aware.\"\necho \"\"\n\n# The current create_app design in HTTPController expects a service to be passed.\n# Running `flask run` with FLASK_APP only looks for an 'app' instance or 'create_app' function\n# without arguments.\n# So, we'll create a temporary run script for demonstration purposes.\n\nTMP_APP_FILE=\"temp_run_http_app.py\"\n\ncat << EOF > \"$TMP_APP_FILE\"\n# This is a temporary file generated by run_local_server.sh for demonstration.\n# In a real deployment, you would have a dedicated app.py/wsgi.py.\n\nfrom stringutils.config import get_config\nfrom stringutils.core import PrefixGenerator\nfrom stringutils.repositories import InMemoryCacheRepository, FileCacheRepository\nfrom stringutils.services import PrefixService\nfrom stringutils.validators import StringValidator\nfrom stringutils.controllers import HTTPController\n\nconfig = get_config()\ngenerator = PrefixGenerator()\nvalidator = StringValidator()\n\n# You can choose your repository here:\n# repository = InMemoryCacheRepository(max_size=config[\"DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE\"])\nrepository = FileCacheRepository(file_path=config[\"DEFAULT_PERSIST_FILE\"])\n\nservice = PrefixService(generator, repository, validator, config)\napp = HTTPController().create_app(service)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    print(\"Serving HTTP API on http://127.0.0.1:5000\")\n    print(\"Example: curl http://127.0.0.1:5000/prefixes?string=test\")\n    app.run(debug=True)\nEOF\n\npython \"$TMP_APP_FILE\"\n\n# Clean up temporary file\nrm \"$TMP_APP_FILE\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Server stopped.\"\n```"}
