dian-app compute \"[10.5, 20.2, 5.1]\"\n# Output: {'median': 10.5, 'count': 3, 'id': 2}\n```\n\nTo prevent saving the computation to history:\n\n```bash\nmedian-app compute --no-save \"1,2,3\"\n# Output: {'median': 2, 'count': 3}\n```\n\n### REST API\n\nStart the API server:\n\n```bash\npoetry run uvicorn median_app.api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\nThe server will run on `http://0.0.0.0:8000`.\n\n#### Endpoints:\n\n**1. POST /median**\n\nComputes the median for the provided list of values and persists the record.\n\n- **URL**: `/median`\n- **Method**: `POST`\n- **Content-Type**: `application/json`\n- **Request Body Example**:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"values\": [3, 1, 2, 4, 5],\n    \"persist\": true\n  }\n  ```\n  `persist` is optional and defaults to `true`.\n- **Successful Response (200 OK) Example**:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"median\": 3,\n    \"id\": 1,\n    \"count\": 5\n  }\n  ```\n- **Error Response (400 Bad Request) Example**:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"detail\": \"Empty list is not allowed\"\n  }\n  ```\n\n**2. GET /history**\n\nRetrieves a list of past computation records.\n\n- **URL**: `/history`\n- **Method**: `GET`\n- **Query Parameters**:\n  - `limit`: (Optional) An integer specifying the maximum number of recent records to retrieve. Defaults to 100.\n    Example: `/history?limit=50`\n- **Successful Response (200 OK) Example**:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"records\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": 1,\n        \"timestamp\": \"2023-10-27T10:00:00.000000\",\n        \"input\": [3, 1, 2, 4, 5],\n        \"median\": 3,\n        \"count\": 5\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n  ```\n\n### Programmatic Use\n\nYou can import and use the median calculator and other components directly in your Python code:\n\n```python\nfrom median_app.median_calculator import MedianCalculator\nfrom median_app.input_validator import InputValidator, InputValidationError\nfrom median_app.db_connection import DBConnection\nfrom median_app.history_repository import HistoryRepository\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport json\n\n# Median Calculator\ncalculator = MedianCalculator()\nresult = calculator.compute([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\nprint(f\"Median: {result}\") # Output: Median: 3\n\n# Input Validator\nvalidator = InputValidator(allow_str_parse=True)\ntry:\n    validated_list = validator.validate_list(\"10,20,30,40\")\n    print(f\"Validated list: {validated_list}\") # Output: Validated list: [10, 20, 30, 40]\nexcept InputValidationError as e:\n    print(f\"Validation Error: {e}\")\n\n# Persistence\ndb = DBConnection(\"my_median_history.db\")\ndb.initialize_schema()\nrepo = HistoryRepository(db)\n\n# Create a dummy record\n# new_record = ComputationRecord(\n#     id=None,\n#     timestamp=datetime.now(),\n#     input_json=json.dumps([1,2,3]),\n#     median=2.0,\n#     count=3\n# )\n# record_id = repo.save(new_record)\n# print(f\"Saved record with ID: {record_id}\")\n\nrecent_records = repo.list_recent(limit=5)\nfor record in recent_records:\n    print(f\"Record: {record.to_dict()}\")\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Setup Dev Environment\n\n```bash\npoetry install --group dev\npoetry shell\n```\n\n### Running Tests\n\n*(Note: Test files are not provided in this generation due to specific instructions, but this section explains how they would be run.)*\n\n```bash\npytest\npytest --cov=src/median_app\n```\n\n### Linting and Formatting\n\n```bash\nblack src/ median_app/\nisort src/ median_app/\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 median_app/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 api.py              # FastAPI application setup\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 api_controller.py   # Business logic for API endpoints\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 cli.py              # CLI entrypoint\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 cli_controller.py   # Business logic for CLI commands\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 computation_record.py # Data model for median computations\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2