port FibonacciError\n\ndef main(db_path: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Initializes the SQLite cache database at the given path.\n    This creates the 'cache' table if it doesn't already exist.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(f\"Attempting to initialize SQLite cache database at: {db_path}\")\n    repo = None\n    try:\n        repo = CacheRepository(db_path=db_path)\n        print(\"SQLite cache database initialized successfully.\")\n    except FibonacciError as e:\n        print(f\"Error initializing SQLite cache: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n    finally:\n        if repo:\n            repo.close()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    if len(sys.argv) < 2:\n        print(\"Usage: python -m tools.migrate_cache <path_to_sqlite_db>\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n    \n    db_file_path = sys.argv[1]\n    main(db_file_path)\n\n```\n\n---\nBelow is the implementation of the `fib` function that strictly adheres to the \"CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS\" section from the problem statement's end.\n\n```python\ndef fib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return n-th Fibonacci number.\n    Uses an iterative approach for calculation.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b\n```"}
