{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "```python\ndef fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return n-th Fibonacci number using the fast-doubling matrix exponentiation method.\n    This method computes F(n) in O(log n) time.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _fast_doubling(k: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        # Computes the k-th and (k+1)-th Fibonacci numbers, (F_k, F_{k+1}).\n        if k == 0:\n            return (0, 1)\n\n        a, b = _fast_doubling(k // 2)\n        c = a * (2 * b - a)\n        d = a * a + b * b\n\n        if k % 2 == 0:\n            return (c, d)\n        else:\n            return (d, c + d)\n\n    return _fast_doubling(n)[0]\n```"}
