       poetry run isort --check src/\n        poetry run flake8 src/\n    - name: Run tests (Note: Tests are not generated as per output constraints)\n      run: |\n        echo \"Tests would run here if they were part of the generated output.\"\n        # poetry run pytest src/monotonic_checker/tests/\n\"\"\"\n\n# README.md\n# Simple README for the project.\n\n\"\"\"\n# Monotonic Checker Service\n\nThis project provides a service to determine if a sequence of comparable values is monotonic (either non-decreasing or non-increasing). It offers both a Command Line Interface (CLI) for interactive use and a lightweight REST API for integration into data pipelines. Check history is recorded to a local SQLite database for auditing.\n\n## Features\n\n-   **Monotonicity Check**: Determine if a sequence is non-decreasing, non-increasing, constant, or not monotonic.\n-   **CLI**: `monotonic-check` command to pass sequences and get results.\n-   **REST API**: `/check` endpoint to POST sequences and receive JSON results.\n-   **Persistence**: Stores check results in a local SQLite database.\n-   **Optional Strictness**: Flag to enforce strict monotonicity (no equal adjacent elements).\n\n## Installation\n\n(Details for installation with Poetry or pip would go here)\n\n## Usage\n\n### CLI\n\n`monotonic-check -s \"[1,2,3,4]\" --strict`\n`monotonic-check -s \"1,1,2,3\"`\n\n### API\n\n(Details for running the Flask app and example `curl` commands would go here)\n\n## Development\n\n(Details for setting up a dev environment and running tests would go here)\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/monotonic_checker/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nPackage initialization for monotonic_checker.\nExposes core components and defines package metadata.\n\"\"\"\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\n# Public API might be imported here, e.g.,\n# from .services import MonotonicService\n# from .repository import SQLiteRepository\n# from .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\n```python\n# src/monotonic_checker/config.py\nimport os\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n\"\"\"\nConfiguration and constants for the Monotonic Checker application.\nAllows overriding some settings via environment variables.\n\"\"\"\n\nDB_PATH: str = os.getenv(\"MONOTONIC_DB_PATH\", \"monotonic_checks.db\")\nMAX_SEQUENCE_LENGTH: int = int(os.getenv(\"MONOTONIC_MAX_SEQUENCE_LENGTH\", \"10000\"))\nAPI_TOKEN: Optional[str] = os.getenv(\"MONOTONIC_API_TOKEN\")\nDEFAULT_STRICT: bool = os.getenv(\"MONOTONIC_DEFAULT_STRICT\", \"False\").lower() == \"true\"\n```python\n# src/monotonic_checker/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"\nCustom exceptions for specific error conditions within the application.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass ValidationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when input data fails validation rules.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass PersistenceError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when there is an issue interacting with the persistence layer.\"\"\"\n    pass\n```python\n# src/monotonic_checker/models.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Any, List, Optional\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .config import MAX_SEQUENCE_LENGTH\n\n\"\"\"\nData Transfer Objects (DTOs) and data models used across different layers\nof the application, ensuring type safety and structured data handling.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass Sequence:\n    \"\"\"\n    Represents an input sequence for monotonicity checking.\n    Validates length and type of items if they are provided as a raw list.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, items: List[Any], strict: bool = False) -> None:\n        self.items = items\n        self.strict = strict\n        self.validate()\n\n    def validate(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates the properties of the sequence.\n        Raises ValidationError if the sequence length exceeds limits.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(self.items, list):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Sequence items must be a list.\")\n        if len(self.items) > MAX_SEQUENCE_LENGTH:\n            raise ValidationError(\n                f\"Sequence too long. Max length is {MAX_SEQUENCE_LENGTH}.\"\n            )\n        # Further type validation of individual items is done in utils.compare.\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass CheckRecord:\n    \"\"\"\n    Represents a stored record of a monotonicity check.\n    Used for persistence and history tracking.\n    \"\"\"\n    id: Optional[int]\n    sequence_json: str\n    is_monotonic: bool\n    direction: str  # 'increasing', 'decreasing', 'constant', 'none'\n    strict: bool\n    created_at: str  # ISO-8601 timestamp string\n```python\n# src/monotonic_checker/utils.py\nimport json\nfrom typing import Any, List\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .config import MAX_SEQUENCE_LENGTH\n\n\"\"\"\nUtility functions for parsing input sequences and performing safe comparisons.\nThese helpers ensure consistent data processing and error handling.\n\"\"\"\n\ndef parse_sequence(raw: Any) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parses a raw input (string or list) into a standardized list of comparable values.\n    Supports JSON array strings, CSV strings, or direct Python lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    items: List[Any]\n    if isinstance(raw, list):\n        items = raw\n    elif isinstance(raw, str):\n        s = raw.strip()\n        if s.startswith('[') and s.endswith(']'):\n            try:\n                items = json.loads(s)\n                if not isinstance(items, list):\n                    raise ValueError(\"JSON string did not yield a list.\")\n            except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n                raise ValidationError(f\"Malformed JSON sequence string: {e}\")\n        elif ',' in s:\n            items = []\n            for item_str in s.split(','):\n                item_str_stripped = item_str.strip()\n                try:\n                    items.append(int(item_str_stripped))\n                except ValueError:\n                    try:\n                        items.append(float(item_str_stripped))\n                    except ValueError:\n                        items.append(item_str_stripped) # Keep as string if not number\n        else:\n            # If it's a single item string without commas or brackets, treat it as a list of one\n            try:\n                items.append(int(s))\n            except ValueError:\n                try:\n                    items.append(float(s))\n                except ValueError:\n                    items.append(s)\n            items = [s] # Treat as a single item list\n    else:\n        raise ValidationError(f\"Unsupported sequence input type: {type(raw)}\")\n\n    if len(items) > MAX_SEQUENCE_LENGTH:\n        raise ValidationError(f\"Sequence too long. Max length is {MAX_SEQUENCE_LENGTH}.\")\n    return items\n\n\ndef compare(a: Any, b: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs a three-way comparison between two values.\n    Returns -1 if a < b, 0 if a == b, and 1 if a > b.\n    Raises ValidationError if values are not comparable.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        if a < b:\n            return -1\n        if a > b:\n            return 1\n        return 0\n    except TypeError as e:\n        raise ValidationError(f\"Values are not comparable: {a!r} and {b!r}. Error: {e}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise ValidationError(f\"An unexpected error occurred during comparison: {e}\")\n\n```python\n# src/monotonic_checker/repository.py\nimport sqlite3\nimport datetime\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom .models import CheckRecord\nfrom .exceptions import PersistenceError\n\n\"\"\"\nPersistence layer for storing and retrieving check history using SQLite.\nHandles database initialization and CRUD operations for CheckRecord objects.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass SQLiteRepository:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages interactions with the SQLite database for CheckRecord persistence.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str) -> None:\n        self._db_path = db_path\n        self._conn: Optional[sqlite3.Connection] = None\n\n    def _get_db_connection(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        \"\"\"Establishes and returns a database connection.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            conn = sqlite3.connect(self._db_path)\n            conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row  # Access columns by name\n            return conn\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to connect to database: {e}\")\n\n    def initialize(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the database by creating the 'checks' table and an index\n        if they do not already exist.\n        \"\"\"\n        with self._get_db_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            try:\n                cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS checks (\n                        id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                        sequence_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n                        is_monotonic BOOLEAN NOT NULL,\n                        direction TEXT NOT NULL,\n                        strict BOOLEAN NOT NULL,\n                        created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n                    );\n                \"\"\")\n                cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                    CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_checks_created_at ON checks(created_at DESC);\n                \"\"\")\n                conn.commit()\n            except sqlite3.Error as e:\n                raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to initialize database: {e}\")\n\n    def save_check(self, record: CheckRecord) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Inserts a new CheckRecord into the database and returns its generated ID.\n        \"\"\"\n        with self._get_db_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            try:\n                cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                    INSERT INTO checks (sequence_json, is_monotonic, direction, strict, created_at)\n                    VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?);\n                \"\"\", (\n                    record.sequence_json,\n                    int(record.is_monotonic),  # SQLite stores bool as int\n                    record.direction,\n                    int(record.strict),      # SQLite stores bool as int\n                    record.created_at\n                ))\n                conn.commit()\n                return cursor.lastrowid\n            except sqlite3.Error as e:\n                raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to save check record: {e}\")\n\n    def list_recent(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[CheckRecord]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieves a list of the most recent CheckRecord entries from the database.\n        \"\"\"\n        with self._get_db_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            try:\n                cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                    SELECT id, sequence_json, is_monotonic, direction, strict, created_at\n                    FROM checks\n                    ORDER BY created_at DESC\n                    LIMIT ?;\n                \"\"\", (limit,))\n                rows = cursor.fetchall()\n                records = []\n                for row in rows:\n                    records.append(CheckRecord(\n                        id=row['id'],\n                        sequence_json=row['sequence_json'],\n                        is_monotonic=bool(row['is_monotonic']),\n                        direction=row['direction'],\n                        strict=bool(row['strict']),\n                        created_at=row['created_at']\n                    ))\n                return records\n            except sqlite3.Error as e:\n                raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to retrieve recent checks: {e}\")\n```python\n# src/monotonic_checker/services.py\nfrom typing import Any, List, Optional, Tuple\nimport datetime\nfrom .utils import compare\nfrom .models import CheckRecord\nfrom .repository import SQLiteRepository\n\n\"\"\"\nCore application logic for determining monotonicity of sequences.\nThis service encapsulates the algorithm and orchestrates persistence.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass MonotonicService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides methods to check sequence monotonicity and record results.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, repo: Optional[SQLiteRepository] = None) -> None:\n        self._repo = repo\n\n    def _is_non_decreasing(self, items: List[Any], strict: bool) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the sequence is non-decreasing (or strictly increasing if strict=True).\"\"\"\n        for i in range(1, len(items)):\n            cmp_val = compare(items[i-1], items[i])\n            if cmp_val > 0:  # Current item is smaller than previous\n                return False\n            if strict and cmp_val == 0:  # Equality not allowed for strict increase\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _is_non_increasing(self, items: List[Any], strict: bool) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the sequence is non-increasing (or strictly decreasing if strict=True).\"\"\"\n        for i in range(1, len(items)):\n            cmp_val = compare(items[i-1], items[i])\n            if cmp_val < 0:  # Current item is larger than previous\n                return False\n            if strict and cmp_val == 0:  # Equality not allowed for strict decrease\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def is_monotonic(self, items: List[Any], strict: bool = False) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if a sequence of comparable values is monotonic.\n        Returns a tuple: (is_monotonic: bool, direction: str).\n        Direction can be 'increasing', 'decreasing', 'constant', or 'none'.\n        \"\"\"\n        n = len(items)\n        if n <= 1:\n            return True, \"constant\"\n\n        is_nd = self._is_non_decreasing(items, strict)\n        is_ni = self._is_non_increasing(items, strict)\n\n        if is_nd and is_ni: # Applies to empty, single-element, or all-equal sequences\n            return True, \"constant\"\n        elif is_nd:\n            return True, \"increasing\"\n        elif is_ni:\n            return True, \"decreasing\"\n        else:\n            return False, \"none\"\n\n    def check_and_record(self, items: List[Any], strict: bool = False) -> CheckRecord:\n        \"\"\"\n        Performs a monotonicity check and optionally records the result in the repository.\n        Returns the CheckRecord generated for this operation.\n        \"\"\"\n        is_mono, direction = self.is_monotonic(items, strict)\n\n        # Truncate sequence_json if it's too long for storage or logging purposes.\n        # This could be more sophisticated (e.g., store hash + metadata for large sequences)\n        sequence_json = str(items) # Basic conversion for storage\n        if len(sequence_json) > 1000: # Example arbitrary limit for representation in DB\n            sequence_json = sequence_json[:997] + \"...\"\n\n        rec = CheckRecord(\n            id=None,\n            sequence_json=sequence_json,\n            is_monotonic=is_mono,\n            direction=direction,\n            strict=strict,\n            created_at=datetime.datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\n        )\n        if self._repo:\n            rec.id = self._repo.save_check(rec)\n        return rec\n```python\n# src/monotonic_checker/cli.py\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom .utils import parse_sequence\nfrom .services import MonotonicService\nfrom .repository import SQLiteRepository\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom .config import DB_PATH, DEFAULT_STRICT\n\n\"\"\"\nCommand Line Interface (CLI) controller for the Monotonic Checker.\nHandles argument parsing, calls the service layer, and prints results.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages the CLI interactions for the monotonic checker.\n    \"\"\"\n    def run(self, argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses CLI arguments, performs the monotonicity check, and prints results.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for errors).\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"monotonic-check\",\n            description=\"Determine if a sequence of values is monotonic.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--sequence\", \"-s\",\n            required=True,\n            help=\"The sequence to check, e.g., '[1,2,3]' or '1,2,3' or '1 2 3'\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--strict\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            default=DEFAULT_STRICT,\n            help=\"Enforce strict monotonicity (no equal adjacent elements).\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--no-persist\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Do not persist the check result to the database.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--history\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"List recent check history.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--limit\",\n            type=int,\n            default=10,\n            help=\"Limit for history listing (default: 10).\"\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        repo = None\n        try:\n            if not args.no_persist or args.history:\n                repo = SQLiteRepository(DB_PATH)\n                repo.initialize()\n        except PersistenceError as e:\n            print(json.dumps({\"error\": f\"Database initialization error: {e}\"}), file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3 # Persistence error\n\n        if args.history:\n            if repo is None:\n                print(json.dumps({\"error\": \"Cannot list history when persistence is disabled.\"}), file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1\n            try:\n                history_records = repo.list_recent(args.limit)\n                output = []\n                for rec in history_records:\n                    output.append({\n                        \"id\": rec.id,\n                        \"sequence_json\": rec.sequence_json,\n                        \"is_monotonic\": rec.is_monotonic,\n                        \"direction\": rec.direction,\n                        \"strict\": rec.strict,\n                        \"created_at\": rec.created_at\n                    })\n                print(json.dumps({\"history\": output}, indent=2))\n                return 0\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                print(json.dumps({\"error\": f\"Failed to retrieve history: {e}\"}), file=sys.stderr)\n                return 3\n\n\n        try:\n            items = parse_sequence(args.sequence)\n            svc = MonotonicService(repo)\n            rec = svc.check_and_record(items, args.strict)\n\n            output = {\n                \"is_monotonic\": rec.is_monotonic,\n                \"direction\": rec.direction,\n                \"record_id\": rec.id\n            }\n            print(json.dumps(output, indent=2))\n            return 0\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            print(json.dumps({\"error\": f\"Validation error: {e}\"}), file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2  # Input validation error\n        except PersistenceError as e:\n            print(json.dumps({\"error\": f\"Persistence error: {e}\"}), file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3  # Persistence error\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(json.dumps({\"error\": f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\"}), file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1  # General error\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the CLI application.\"\"\"\n    return CLIController().run(argv)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    sys.exit(main())\n```python\n# src/monotonic_checker/api.py\nfrom flask import Flask, request, jsonify, Response\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Optional\nimport logging\n\nfrom .services import MonotonicService\nfrom .repository import SQLiteRepository\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom .config import DB_PATH, API_TOKEN, DEFAULT_STRICT\n\n\"\"\"\nREST API controller for the Monotonic Checker using Flask.\nProvides endpoints for checking monotonicity and viewing history.\n\"\"\"\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef create_app(config_overrides: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None) -> Flask:\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates and configures the Flask application instance.\n    Allows for configuration overrides, primarily for testing.\n    \"\"\"\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n\n    # Apply configuration overrides\n    if config_overrides:\n        for key, value in config_overrides.items():\n            globals()[key] = value # This is a simple way for demo, proper app.config is better\n\n    try:\n        repo = SQLiteRepository(DB_PATH)\n        repo.initialize()\n        service = MonotonicService(repo)\n    except PersistenceError as e:\n        logger.error(f\"Failed to initialize database for API: {e}\")\n        # In a production setup, this might prevent the app from starting or\n        # trigger a circuit breaker. For now, log and allow it to fail on call.\n        service = MonotonicService(None) # Operate without persistence\n        app.config['DB_UNAVAILABLE'] = True\n    else:\n        app.config['DB_UNAVAILABLE'] = False\n\n    @app.errorhandler(ValidationError)\n    def handle_validation_error(error: ValidationError) -> Response:\n        \"\"\"Error handler for ValidationError, returning a 400 Bad Request.\"\"\"\n        logger.warning(f\"Validation error: {error}\")\n        return jsonify({\"error\": \"Validation error\", \"details\": str(error)}), 400\n\n    @app.errorhandler(PersistenceError)\n    def handle_persistence_error(error: PersistenceError) -> Response:\n        \"\"\"Error handler for PersistenceError, returning a 500 Internal Server Error.\"\"\"\n        logger.error(f\"Persistence error: {error}\")\n        return jsonify({\"error\": \"Persistence error\", \"details\": str(error)}), 500\n\n    @app.errorhandler(Exception)\n    def handle_generic_error(error: Exception) -> Response:\n        \"\"\"Generic error handler for unexpected exceptions, returning a 500.\"\"\"\n        logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred during API request.\")\n        return jsonify({\"error\": \"Internal server error\"}), 500\n\n    def _require_api_token() -> Optional[Response]:\n        \"\"\"Helper to enforce API token authentication.\"\"\"\n        if API_TOKEN:\n            token = request.headers.get(\"X-API-Token\")\n            if not token or token != API_TOKEN:\n                logger.warning(\"API token missing or invalid.\")\n                return jsonify({\"error\": \"Missing or invalid API token\"}), 401\n        return None\n\n    @app.route(\"/check\", methods=[\"POST\"])\n    def check_sequence() -> Response:\n        \"\"\"\n        POST /check: Determines monotonicity of a sequence and records the check.\n        Requires JSON body with \"sequence\" (array) and optional \"strict\" (boolean).\n        \"\"\"\n        auth_error = _require_api_token()\n        if auth_error:\n            return auth_error\n\n        body = request.get_json(force=True)\n        if not body or \"sequence\" not in body:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Request body must contain 'sequence' array.\")\n\n        sequence_items = body.get(\"sequence\")\n        if not isinstance(sequence_items, list):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Value for 'sequence' must be an array.\")\n\n        strict_flag = body.get(\"strict\", DEFAULT_STRICT)\n        if not isinstance(strict_flag, bool):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Value for 'strict' must be a boolean.\")\n\n        record = service.check_and_record(sequence_items, strict_flag)\n\n        response_data = {\n            \"is_monotonic\": record.is_monotonic,\n            \"direction\": record.direction,\n            \"record_id\": record.id\n        }\n        return jsonify(response_data), 200\n\n    @app.route(\"/history\", methods=[\"GET\"])\n    def get_history() -> Response:\n        \"\"\"\n        GET /history: Retrieves recent check history.\n        Requires API token if configured. Accepts optional 'limit' query parameter.\n        \"\"\"\n        auth_error = _require_api_token()\n        if auth_error:\n            return auth_error\n\n        if app.config['DB_UNAVAILABLE']:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"History unavailable: Database not initialized.\"}), 500\n\n        try:\n            limit = int(request.args.get(\"limit\", 10))\n            if limit <= 0:\n                raise ValidationError(\"Limit must be a positive integer.\")\n        except ValueError:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Invalid 'limit' parameter, must be an integer.\")\n\n        records = repo.list_recent(limit)\n        history_data = []\n        for rec in records:\n            history_data.append({\n                \"id\": rec.id,\n                \"sequence_json\": rec.sequence_json,\n                \"is_monotonic\": rec.is_monotonic,\n                \"direction\": rec.direction,\n                \"strict\": rec.strict,\n                \"created_at\": rec.created_at\n            })\n        return jsonify({\"history\": history_data}), 200\n\n    return app\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app = create_app()\n    app.run(debug=True) # For development, use gunicorn for production\n```"}
